I would say that you could require Best of 13 actually to be all 13
classes, but marvin already seems to be playing that rule.

I would keep Best of 13; I don't think even marvin can do it every year
and there are some other people nibbling at being that good.

But eliminate at least gender as a game-uniqueness criterion. I'd say
alignment as well.

[The way to do this would be a) use game start time as the consecutiveness
criterion and assemble 13 "consecutive" games like this;

For each ascension a player has, count 12 games after that one by taking
the first subsequent game that does not violate the uniqueness criterion.

So, for example, if I ascend a human Valkyrie, the sequence of 12 after
that on which I might be judged for best-of-13 won't be affected by any
more human Valkyries I choose to play (but if I ascend one of them, she
might be considered the start of a series of 13) whether they win or
lose.]

I'd also suggest using starting alignment and gender for the Recognition
Trophies. Starting alignment seriously affects the early game, but
game-ending alignment can be adjusted quite easily.
